    <b>Slax (Music Software)</b><br>
    <hr>
    <i>From Fakepedia, the made up encyclopedia</i><br>
    <div style="margin: 16px;">
        This page is meant for internal use only. If you came here via a link in a page, report this issue in the github repo.
    </div>
    Slax was a music service and music player<super>[1]</super> designed, developed, and maintained by SlinxWare2k4 (Later SlinxWare Software, Inc.<super>[2]</super>) that specialized in various forms of Electronic Music.
    Slax specialized in distributing music made specifically with trackers<super>[3]</super>, but also offered other types of music<super>[4]</super>. Slax was first released for Windows and OS X in 2005, with a web client launching in 2007.
    Slax made it easy to upload music and distribute it<super>[5]</super> globally for free<super>[6]</super>, though the times users had to wait for approval were known to be long<super>[7]</super>.
    SlinxWare Software was bought out by The SL Group in 2011<super>[8]</super>, and Slax was shut down in 2013 with its library being merged and accounts migrated to SL Music<super>[9]</super>.<br>
